{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_third([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_third([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2])\n    [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n    \"\"\"\n    l_prime = list(l) # Create a shallow copy of the input list.\n    divisible_elements = []\n\n    # Extract elements at indices divisible by three.\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            divisible_elements.append(l[i])\n\n    divisible_elements.sort() # Sort the collected elements.\n\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    # Re-insert sorted elements into their original positions.\n    for i in range(len(l_prime)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            l_prime[i] = divisible_elements[sorted_idx]\n            sorted_idx += 1\n\n    return l_prime"}
