{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "def fizz_buzz(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n\n    def _is_divisible_by_11_or_13(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if an integer is divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n        return (num % 11 == 0) or (num % 13 == 0)\n\n    def _count_digit_occurrences(num: int, digit: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the occurrences of a specific digit within an integer.\"\"\"\n        return str(num).count(str(digit))\n\n    total_count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if _is_divisible_by_11_or_13(i):\n            total_count += _count_digit_occurrences(i, 7)\n    return total_count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "def sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_even([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_even([5, 6, 3, 4])\n    [3, 6, 5, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    result_list = list(l) # Create a mutable copy of the input list.\n\n    even_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            even_elements.append(l[i])\n\n    even_elements.sort() # Sort the extracted even elements.\n\n    sorted_even_idx = 0\n    for i in range(len(result_list)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            result_list[i] = even_elements[sorted_even_idx]\n            sorted_even_idx += 1\n\n    return result_list"}
